0..79 Comment "// Access at a place. `access xs.#[i] as w { … }` lends one element of a held"
80..157 Comment "// list to a view: the index is a value read where the access stands, and the"
158..236 Comment "// view is the element at it. An exclusive view writes its element back at its"
237..312 Comment "// index and the rest of the list stands as it was; a shared view reads it."
313..389 Comment "// The held list is lent as a whole, whatever the index, so two views of one"
390..464 Comment "// list stand together only when both are shared. The place follows Rust\'s"
465..541 Comment "// index expression on a place (_The Rust Reference_, § Index expressions)."
543..570 Comment "// The native finite lists."
